METHOD: Built cmd/server (go build, unmodified source) to a scratchpad binary,
ran it with BUDGET_DATA_DIR pointed at a scratch directory OUTSIDE the repo
(/tmp/.../scratchpad/a11y/data), never the repo's own data/. Fixture:
usaa-wide (pattern "usaa") and usaa-narrow (pattern "usaa-checking"), one CSV
usaa-checking-2026.csv that both patterns match, so
accounts.OverlapWarnings runs the real production code path, same setup
class as judge-claude's S4.3 verdict. Drove real Chromium (Playwright
1.62.1): keyboard-only interaction via Tab-walks and .focus()+Enter (never
.click() for the checks that matter), a MutationObserver armed via
addInitScript before any page script runs, and CDP
Accessibility.getFullAXTree for the AX-tree checks -- the specific
instrument my S4.3 audit skipped. Harness/logs:
/tmp/claude-1000/-home-darrell-work-agents2/f76f0c6a-1d57-487c-9d1f-12155a9b3cb0/scratchpad/a11y/pw/{harness.js,followup.js,followup2.js,axe_noWarnings.js}
axe-core 4.10 run in-page against both themes, warnings present and absent.
Only file written inside the repo is this verdict.

POINT 16, SEQUENCE 1 (dismiss -> resolve -> recreate the SAME overlap).
Keyboard-only throughout: Tab-walked from page load to the dismiss button
(11 tabs), Enter to dismiss; Control+A + retype in the pattern textarea,
Tab to "Save changes", Enter, twice (resolve then recreate).
  initial:        banner=true  dismissBtn=true region="Pattern overlap warning: file \"usaa-checking-2026.csv\" ..."
  after dismiss:   banner=false region="Pattern overlap warning dismissed." storedKey=9d511a0b...
  after resolve:   banner=false region="Pattern overlap warning dismissed." storedKey=null dataKey=""
  after recreate:  banner=true  dismissBtn=true region="Pattern overlap warning: file \"usaa-checking-2026.csv\" ..." storedKey=null dataKey=9d511a0b...
  bannerVisibleText at recreate == regionText at recreate (byte match, modulo the trailing footnote paragraph).
A clean second Tab-walk (from a fresh load of the same warning state, since
the DOM after recreate is byte-identical to the DOM at initial load for the
banner block) reached the dismiss button in 10 tabs and Enter dismissed it
correctly -- confirms the recreated banner's control is keyboard-reachable
and operable, not just present in markup.
RULING: PASS. This is the S4-dispute defect (judge-claude's step 4): stale
dismissal key survived a resolve because the old code returned at
`if (!banner) return` before clearing it. Here the key clears when
data-warnings-key is empty (dataKey="" / storedKey=null after resolve), so
the recreate is correctly treated as a new, undismissed warning. Banner,
dismiss control, and matching announcement all return together.

POINT 16, SEQUENCE 2 (dismiss -> ordinary reload, warnings unchanged). This
is the specific check my S4.3 audit substituted with a data-warnings-text
read and got wrong. This time: CDP Accessibility.getFullAXTree() after
dismiss + reload.
  region.textContent after reload = ""  (innerHTML = "")
  banner present = false, dismiss button in DOM = false
  region computed style: role=status, aria-live=polite, still present (not
    removed), sr-only (clip rect(0,0,0,0), 1x1) -- exposed to AT, not
    display:none, and still armed for a future live update
  seq2_axTreeWarningNodes = [] -- ZERO AX nodes anywhere contain "Pattern
    overlap warning" text after dismiss+reload. (Repeated with a role=status
    filter: two status nodes exist post-reload, both name="" -- the error
    region and the warnings region -- neither carries warning text.)
This directly falsifies the defect judge-claude found in S4.3 (two
un-ignored StaticText/InlineTextBox AX nodes asserting the warning with no
visible counterpart). Here there are none.
RULING: PASS.

THE GUARD, ALL DIRECTIONS (MutationObserver armed via addInitScript before
page scripts run, filtered to mutations whose target is/inside
#accounts-warnings-region):
  - Unrelated mutation (edit account NAME only, unrelated to patterns):
    0 mutations on the region. PASS.
  - Genuinely changed warning set (resolve the overlap): exactly 1 mutation,
    region text -> "". PASS (announces once, matches point 14's "on state
    change" and point 16's parity).
  - Warnings clearing leaves the region empty: same event, confirmed
    regionText === "" afterward. PASS.
  - Dismissal re-asserted on load: reload after dismiss (same session,
    warnings unchanged) produced 2 region mutations -- server-rendered full
    warning text (parser insertion), then the script's JS write to "".
    Checked document.readyState at both: both fire at readyState="loading",
    i.e. within the initial synchronous parse/script-execution window,
    before DOMContentLoaded and before any AT would have flushed an
    announcement for the intermediate state. Final, settled state is the
    correct "" — matches the AX-tree-empty result in sequence 2. This is the
    same mechanism judge-claude's S4.3 dissent described (readyState=loading
    for both edits) but there the FINAL state was still wrong; here it
    converges correctly. Also checked the ordinary case (no dismissal,
    unchanged warnings, plain reload): exactly 1 mutation (the parse-time
    insertion of the still-correct warning text) and 0 extra JS-triggered
    writes — syncWarnings' same-text guard correctly no-ops when nothing
    changed. PASS on all four directions.

POINT 14 (still holds). Keyboard dismissal: confirmed above (Tab + Enter,
twice, from two different starting states). In-session persistence:
dismiss -> reload keeps banner suppressed (sequence 2). Reappearance on a
changed set: sequence 1's recreate step, and the guard's "changed warning
set" check. Nothing across sessions: every fresh browser context (fresh
sessionStorage) in every test below shows the banner and full warning text
on first load -- dismissal never leaks across sessions. Server computation
never suppressed: data-warnings-key/data-warnings-text carry the full,
correct warning on every response regardless of client dismissal state
(confirmed in sequence 2's afterReload.dataKey, and directly in the No-JS
test below, where nothing client-side ever runs). PASS.

POINT 10 (dismiss announces result, focus lands sensibly). Fresh load,
focus() the dismiss button directly, Enter:
  regionText = "Pattern overlap warning dismissed."
  activeElementId = "accounts-new-heading" (an <h2>, tabindex=-1'd by the
    handler), activeElementIsBody = false.
PASS -- a real result announcement, and focus does not fall back to <body>.

POINTS 7/12 (contrast, both themes, warning text + dismiss icon). Measured
via getComputedStyle + WCAG relative-luminance contrast, not eyeballed:
  light: warning label/list text  rgb(180,83,9) on rgb(255,251,235) = 4.84:1
         dismiss icon (svg stroke=currentColor, same class)          = 4.84:1
         footnote text (amber-700 on amber-50)                       = 4.84:1
  dark:  warning label/list text  rgb(252,211,77) on rgb(120,53,15) = 6.29:1
         dismiss icon             rgb(251,191,36) on rgb(120,53,15) = 5.43:1
         footnote text (amber-400 on dark amber-900/30 composited)   = 5.43:1
All clear the 4.5:1 text floor (point 7) in both themes (point 12 parity);
dismiss icon clears the 3:1 UI-component floor with margin in both themes.
Matches the template's own inline comment (amber-700 not amber-600) and
independently confirms it rather than trusting the comment. PASS.

FULL AXE SCAN, both themes, warnings present and absent (axe-core 4.10,
wcag2a/wcag2aa/wcag21aa/wcag22aa tags), 4 scans total:
  light+warnings-present: 1 violation (color-contrast, serious) on the two
