  dark+warnings-present:  same 2 nodes, same pre-existing violation.
  light+warnings-absent (overlap resolved via a live POST, then restored):
    same 2 nodes, same violation, nothing new.
  dark+warnings-absent:   same.
No new violation in any of the four scans. PASS.

NO-JS BEHAVIOUR. New context with javaScriptEnabled: false, full page load:
  bannerPresent=true, dismissBtnPresent=true (button renders, inert without
    JS -- acceptable, dismissal is documented progressive enhancement)
  regionText === bannerText content (both server-rendered, both carry the
    identical current warning, both always visible/exposed)
PASS -- with JS off the warning is visible, the region's content is present
and matches what's shown; there is no divergence to have, since dismissal
(the only thing that could desync them) never executes.

OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking).
- After the "resolve" step in sequence 1 (dismiss, then an edit that clears
  the overlap), the region is left holding the stale "Pattern overlap
  warning dismissed." text rather than being cleared, because
  lastWarningsText is already '' from the dismiss handler and the newly-
  resolved effectiveText also computes to '', so the same-text guard no-ops
  and the write never happens. This is not a point-16 violation -- the text
  is a true, past-tense statement and nothing on screen contradicts it, so
  no active condition is being asserted without a visible counterpart -- but
  it is slightly stale UX for an AT user who navigates back into that region
  later in the session. Worth a follow-up ticket, not a FAIL here.
- Did not independently verify S5's Go-test-quality sub-items (b)-(e); that
  is checker-tests's lane.

VERDICT: PASS. Both contested S4.3 sequences reproduce correctly fixed under
the same instrumentation that found them broken (real browser, keyboard-only
interaction, CDP AX-tree read before/after, MutationObserver armed pre-load).
ACCESSIBILITY.md points 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, and the new point 16 all hold on
accounts.html as changed by S5.
